<article class="env-lemma" id="0F8F">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0F8F">Lemma <span data-tag="0F8F">36.37.2</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a quasi-compact and quasi-separated scheme with the resolution property. Then every perfect object of $D(\mathcal{O}_ X)$ can be represented by a bounded complex of finite locally free $\mathcal{O}_ X$-modules. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $E$ be a perfect object of $D(\mathcal{O}_ X)$. By Lemma <a href="/tag/0F8C" data-tag="0F8C">36.36.10</a> we see that $X$ has affine diagonal. Hence by Proposition <a href="/tag/08DB" data-tag="08DB">36.7.5</a> we can represent $E$ by a complex $\mathcal{F}^\bullet $ of quasi-coherent $\mathcal{O}_ X$-modules. Observe that $E$ is in $D^ b(\mathcal{O}_ X)$ because $X$ is quasi-compact. Hence $\tau _{\geq n}\mathcal{F}^\bullet $ is a bounded below complex of quasi-coherent $\mathcal{O}_ X$-modules which represents $E$ if $n \ll 0$. Thus we may apply Lemma <a href="/tag/0F8E" data-tag="0F8E">36.37.1</a> to conclude. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>